@startuml Leader Address Access

title The Convoy Leader reads destination addresses: scoped, time-limited, audited
caption Target design. Decisions X7, X9, X11, X12, X13, O26, O1. ADRs 0009, 0010. Implementation is gated by a security review.

autonumber

actor "Convoy Leader" as leader
actor Dispatcher as disp
actor "Ground Officer" as go
participant "Checklist page\n(phone)" as page
participant "Freedom API" as api
database "dbo\n(route, convoy)" as dbo
database "sensitive schema\n(Receiver detail + access log)" as sens

== Before the window opens (more than 14 days before planned departure) ==
leader -> page : open checklist
page -> api : GET /convoys/{id}/addresses
api -> dbo : is the caller the current leader of this convoy?
api --> page : route point **headers only** (name and kind)

== Inside the window ==
leader -> page : reveal addresses
page -> leader : re-authenticate
leader -> page : re-authenticated
page -> api : GET /convoys/{id}/addresses
api -> dbo : current leader of this convoy? window open?\nconvoy not arrived?
group one transaction, through the sensitive connection
  api -> sens : write access-log row (reader capacity: Convoy Leader, convoy id)
  api -> sens : read addresses of **all Receivers on this convoy**
end
api --> page : route and Receiver addresses\n(Cache-Control: no-store)
note right of page
  Shown on this page only. Never printed, logged, queued,
  or put on a manifest, label or filing sheet.
  Nothing kept on the device.
end note

== Refusals ==
alt a leader of another convoy
  page -> api : GET /convoys/{other}/addresses
  api --> page : 403
else after reassignment or arrival
  page -> api : GET /convoys/{id}/addresses
  api --> page : 403 (the window has closed for this person)
else a Dispatcher or other driver
  disp -> api : GET /convoys/{id}/addresses
  api --> disp : 403 (O1)
end

== Oversight ==
go -> api : review receiver access log
api -> sens : read access log
api --> go : every read, by whom, in what capacity, for which convoy

@enduml
